{
  "_help": [
    "THE STANDARD PORTABLE-BUILDING LINE, as Barnwright's 3D designer draws it. What a builder MAKES, shared by every dealer that sells it. NO PRICES live here: every price is in a company's own file.",
    "styles: each style's name, category, roof shape (gable gambrel salt lean slope), wall height in feet, flags (metal, dormer, porch F/S/C, side), traits (kennel, cottage, gambrel shoulders, gableVent, gableBand, rakeOverhang, loft) and loadout (which standard doors and windows it comes with).",
    "loft {ends, depthFt}: which gable ends carry a loft and how deep it is. depthFt 4 at both ends is an ASSUMPTION the owner must confirm (Barnwright never drew a loft).",
    "items: every door, window and fixture: name, kind (door ru win light bench shelf out ilt post), draw (which drawing module draws it), w and h in feet (door widths are the shop's rough openings), leaves, and flags. 'sill' is recorded only because Barnwright's table has it; nothing reads it (a window's height comes from the window-top rule).",
    "palettes: colours as [name, hex]. 'metal' is both the roof colours for every building and the siding colours for metal styles, exactly as in Barnwright.",
    "options: which dormers, ramps, electrical packages, odds and ends and per-square-foot upgrades exist, what they are called, and what they change in the construction. No prices.",
    "Numbers and names here were read live from Barnwright's page (test/golden/barnwright-catalogue.json)."
  ],
